# ============================================================================
# Bab-ilu — Environment Variables
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file:  cp config/.env.example .env
# Then fill in the values below. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Summary:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  — handled by Claude Code (run `claude login`)
#   LLM_*              — optional, enables a second-opinion Review LLM
#   IMAGE_GEN_*        — optional, enables aesthetic-warburg /prompt --test
#                        (reverse-prompt image generation + vision scoring)
# ============================================================================


# --- Anthropic API Key (managed by Claude Code) -----------------------------
# All Bab-ilu LLM reasoning runs inside the Claude Code session, not via a
# Python-side SDK call. Run:
#   claude login
# Claude Code handles authentication for you. No manual export needed.


# --- Review LLM (Optional — enables cross-model MCP review) -----------------
# What it does: a second LLM (independent of Claude) reviews artifacts via
# the mcp-servers/llm-review MCP server. The reviewer critiques without
# seeing Claude's prior analysis, improving quality via independence.
#
# Used by:   mcp-servers/llm-review/server.py
# Without it: the MCP server simply refuses to start; no Bab-ilu skill
#             depends on this being configured. Safe to leave blank.
#
# Works with any OpenAI-compatible API. Common providers:
#
#   Provider      | LLM_BASE_URL                                        | Example LLM_MODEL
#   ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | -----------------
#   DeepSeek      | https://api.deepseek.com/v1                         | deepseek-chat
#   OpenAI        | https://api.openai.com/v1                           | gpt-4o
#   OpenRouter    | https://openrouter.ai/api/v1                        | (any model slug)
#   Qwen          | https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1   | qwen-max
#   SiliconFlow   | https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1                       | (see docs)
#
# Setup:
#   1. Get an API key from your chosen provider
#   2. Fill in the three variables below
#   3. Restart Claude Code so the MCP server picks up the new values
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_MODEL=
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=    # Optional: fallback model if primary fails


# --- Image generation (Optional — enables /prompt --test reverse scoring) ---
# What it does: tools/gen_client.py + tools/prompt_tester.py call an
# OpenAI-compatible image endpoint to generate an image from a Bab-ilu
# aesthetic prompt, then ask a vision model to reverse-score how well
# the image lands inside the claimed Pathosformel. This is the
# "abstraction training loop" for the aesthetic-warburg lens — see
# tools/prompt_tester.py module docstring.
#
# Used by:   tools/prompt_tester.py, tools/gen_client.py (via /prompt --test)
# Without these: /prompt still emits four-segment prompts, but --test
#                (reverse-score against AAT/Iconclass/Warburg panel)
#                will raise RuntimeError. /prompt without --test is
#                unaffected and works offline.
#
# Works with any OpenAI-compatible image gateway that exposes either
# `/v1/images/generations` or `/v1/chat/completions` with data-URL image
# responses. Common setups: Gemini image models via OpenRouter / a
# self-hosted proxy / a direct OpenAI account with images scope.
IMAGE_GEN_BASE_URL=
IMAGE_GEN_API_KEY=
# IMAGE_GEN_MODELS=model-a,model-b,model-c   # Optional: comma-separated
                                              # candidate models; falls back
                                              # in declared order.
